| RISC OS on Linux: loads its own modules (discs in RISC OS's format,
| sound, USB and the rest) before the other files here, so that they can
| use them (Configure's SndSetup needs SoundControl for *MixVolume) and so
| that one of them failing can't leave them unloaded. The list is
| Choices:Boot.TestBed; through *X, so that nothing in it failing stops
| the rest of start-up. Keep this file's name: it is first in the
| alphabet so that it runs first.
|
| Also: the current directory is HardDisc4, as RISC OS itself starts in
| the root of the disc it boots from. It was IXFS::ROL.$ (Linux's root),
| where RISC OS can't write, so programs saving there (crash dumps, for
| one) failed.
|
